tly horizontal."], ["Square","Trade term \u2014 Square: A perfect 90-degree corner."], ["On center (OC)","Trade term \u2014 On center (OC): Spacing measured from the center of one member to the next."], ["Sole plate","Trade term \u2014 Sole plate: The bottom horizontal wall framing member."], ["Top plate","Trade term \u2014 Top plate: The top horizontal wall framing member, usually doubled."], ["Header","Trade term \u2014 Header: The beam over doors and windows carrying the load above."], ["Sheathing","Trade term \u2014 Sheathing: Panels covering the frame: plywood or OSB."], ["Miter","Trade term \u2014 Miter: An angled cut joining two pieces at a corner."], ["Coping","Trade term \u2014 Coping: Cutting trim to fit the profile of the adjoining piece."], ["Ripping","Trade term \u2014 Ripping: Cutting wood along the grain."], ["Crosscut","Trade term \u2014 Crosscut: Cutting wood across the grain."], ["Kerf","Trade term \u2014 Kerf: The width of material removed by the saw blade."], ["Stair stringer","Trade term \u2014 Stair stringer: The diagonal board carrying stair treads."]];
